<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="5dp"
    android:height="10dp"
    android:viewportWidth="5"
    android:viewportHeight="10"
    android:autoMirrored="true">
    <!--
      Material Symbols `arrow_right`, cropped to the glyph. The stock asset draws this triangle at
      x[10,15] y[7,17] of a 24x24 viewport, i.e. two thirds of the icon is transparent margin — which
      would make the caller's size the padding knob rather than the chevron knob (bigger chevron =
      more space around it). Translated to a tight 5x10 box so the two are independent: the caller
      sizes the chevron itself and spaces it with real layout. Draw it at a 1:2 box (see
      [SymbolSeparator]); a square one would letterbox the margin straight back in.

      autoMirrored because this chevron means "and then", so it has to follow the reading direction of
      the row it punctuates. The app is LTR-only today (no android:supportsRtl, and es/fi/it/pl are all
      LTR), so nothing mirrors it yet; declaring it on the asset is what keeps that true for free if an
      RTL locale ever lands, rather than leaving the arrow to point back up the trip.
    -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#000000"
        android:pathData="M0,10V0l5,5l-5,5Z"/>
</vector>
